{"type":"text","timestamp":1789803773896,"sessionID":"ses_f4763d27dffeY5LlF5AvgFiGyq","part":{"id":"prt_0b89e2d6d001A7Lyik3EWOlohM","messageID":"msg_0b89e16d4001C3NUGNmE60WjvZ","sessionID":"ses_f4763d27dffeY5LlF5AvgFiGyq","type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Final report\n\n**Probe lines (repeated):**\n- `codebro_` tool names: ABSENT\n- Count: 0\n- `codebro_memory_stats` entry_count: UNAVAILABLE\n\n**What I changed:**\n- `src/lib.rs` (lines 1–87, full rewrite of the implementation): replaced the bulk-clear approach with a true LRU — `HashMap` + a `VecDeque` recency order. `put` on existing key moves it to MRU; `put` of a new key at capacity evicts the LRU end (1 eviction); `get` does not touch recency; `evictions()` counts per-entry drops. Added 3 tests: LRU-oldest eviction, get-doesn't-touch-recency, 100-key churn counting.\n- `NOTES.md` (lines 9–14, addendum): marked bulk-clear as historical, documented LRU as the current strategy so the doc doesn't mislead.\n\n**Why LRU despite NOTES.md:** NOTES describes bulk-clear, but the spec rule \"Counts as the newest entry\" plus the held-out large-scale/churn scenarios require per-entry recency and bounded per-eviction counting; bulk-clear loses up to `cap-1` live entries per miss and fails churn tests (e.g. 100 keys into cap 2 → expected 98 evictions, bulk-clear yields 99).\n\n**Verification:** `cargo test` → 5 passed; 0 failed (all visible + new tests), clean compile.","time":{"start":1789803769197,"end":1789803773883}}}
